# Style Rules (P4) — Documentation & Presentation

## Documentation Sync (DS-*)

### ST-1 — Human-Facing Content Registry (DS-1)

On any iteration that affects users, reviewers, or the public site, review or explicitly confirm N/A for every path in the content registry:
- Primary docs: `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`
- Web demo primary IA: Home (`workflow-system/human/demo/index.html`), System (`framework-chain/`), I/O (`context-flow/`), Harness (`benchmark-results/`), Timeline (`version-timeline/`)
- Web demo compatibility routes: `design-system/`, `framework-chain/`, `context-flow/`, `version-timeline/`, `design-architecture/`, `workflow-visualizer/`, `stage-explorer/`, `benchmark-results/`, `blog/` (historical/editorial only; not current product truth)
- User guides EN: `workflow-system/human/en/` (8 files)
- User guides ZH: `workflow-system/human/zh/` (8 files)
- Design system: `workflow-system/human/demo/shared/` (styles.css, nav.js, i18n.js)
- CI/CD: `.github/workflows/*.yml`
- Build and demo-data pipeline: `scripts/build-site.sh`, `scripts/generate_human_docs.py`, `scripts/generate_demo_seed_catalog.py`

#### Demo Page Consistency Checklist

Before committing changes under `workflow-system/human/demo/`:
1. Every HTML page loads `shared/styles.css`
2. Every HTML page loads `shared/nav.js` and `shared/i18n.js`
3. No ad-hoc colors; use DS-2 palette
4. Every `data-i18n` key exists in both EN and ZH
5. Layout works at 640px width
6. Spot-check all pages at desktop and 640px width

### ST-2 — NieR: Automata Visual Identity (DS-2)

When editing web content under `workflow-system/human/demo/`:
- Colors: Gold accent `#B8860B`, Devola Red `#9B4444`, Warm Parchment `#F0EBE0`
- Typography: Cinzel (headers), Inter (body), JetBrains Mono (code)
- Tone: Warm, guardian-like (Devola), professional
- Consistency: Changes to colors/fonts/spacing on one page must be harmonized across all demo pages

### ST-3 — Bilingual Completeness (DS-3)

Any substantive update to a guide in `workflow-system/human/en/` requires a matching update in `workflow-system/human/zh/` (and vice versa). Adding or changing `data-i18n` keys requires both language dictionaries updated in the same commit.

#### Showcase Page Bilingual Completeness

Every `data-i18n` key in the four showcase pages MUST exist in both `en` and
`zh` blocks of `shared/i18n.js` or page-local `addTranslations` calls before
commit.

### ST-4 — Version Propagation in Human Docs (DS-4)

After bumping version, verify: demo `index.html` "What's New" and all EN/ZH files that mention the version. The `README.md` version badge and the `benchmark-results/index.html` displayed version are render/load-time DERIVED per C-6 (v14.4.0 G-031) — verify the derivation mechanism stays intact, not a literal. Run `make sync-human-docs` and `python -m pytest tests/test_version.py -v`.

#### Version Timeline Propagation

Whenever `__version__` changes, `workflow-system/human/demo/version-timeline/versions.json` MUST gain a new entry in the same PR. Required fields: version, date, era, headline, summary, highlights, metrics. Never invent metrics not stated in CHANGELOG.md.

## Web Experience (WX-*)

### ST-6 — Four Theme Showcases Are Mandatory (WX-1)

The four v6.3 theme pages (design-system, framework-chain, context-flow, version-timeline) are first-class deliverables. None may be removed without explicit retrospective entry, deprecation notice, nav update, and cross-page CTA update in the same PR.

#### Cross-Page CTA Cluster Integrity

The four theme pages MUST cross-link via footer/hero CTA clusters. Each page MUST carry a "Read SKILL" link to the GitHub URL. Minimum: 12 internal cross-links + 4 SKILL receipt links across the four pages.

### ST-8 — Motion Patterns Must Be Showcased (WX-3)

New `@keyframes` in `shared/styles.css` MUST appear as MotionShowcase in `design-system/index.html#ds-motion` in the same PR with: live demo, Replay button, duration/easing badge, i18n key in both EN/ZH, reduced-motion coverage.

#### Design Tokens Must Be Showcased

New CSS custom properties in `:root` MUST have dark-mode values AND a TokenSwatch in `design-system/index.html#ds-palette` in the same PR.

#### Components Must Be Showcased

New component class families in `shared/styles.css` MUST appear in `design-system/index.html#ds-components` with live example, component name in `<code>`, and i18n description.

### ST-11 — SKILL.md Section Changes Cascade to Showcase (WX-6)

When specific SKILL.md sections change, the corresponding showcase page sections MUST be updated verbatim in the same PR per CO-2.
